    "body": "#### Please, fill all relevant items: ####\r\n- [x] I have read CONTRIBUTING.rst\r\n- [x] I have tried with the latest pre-release version and I still can reproduce the issue.\r\n\r\n##### Tribler version/branch+revision: #####\r\nTribler 7 alpha 3\r\n\r\n##### Operating system and version: #####\r\nWindows 7 (x86-64)\r\n\r\n##### Expected behavior: #####\r\nTribler should ask for an ok on installing VLC, as per the [cookielaw](https://cookierecht.nl/cookiewet/ook-installatie-van-additionele-software-valt-onder-de-cookiewet/)\r\n\r\nAlso it doesn't uninstall if I remove tribler.\r\n\r\nAnd I rather expect tribler to use my system default media player (vlc is the 4th one on my system!), and not embed its own. But that is a different issue.\r\n\r\n##### Actual behavior: #####\r\nTribler installs VLC w/o any notification, not approval.\r\n\r\n##### Steps to reproduce the behavior: #####\r\nRun the windows installer for Tribler.\r\n\r\n##### Relevant log file output: #####\r\nN/A",
